  <h2>How does Scout's Human route compare with Scale.jobs on price?</h2>
  <p>On the published figures alone, Scale.jobs is usually cheaper per application than Scout's Human Assistant plans, but its monthly prices depend on add-ons. Its $199 monthly plan lists 500 applications, about $0.40 each by our arithmetic (price divided by applications), and its $149 plan lists 250 applications, about $0.60 each. Those prices leave out two optional paid add-ons, We Find Jobs and AI Custom Resumes, at $99 each on the $199 plan and $79 each on the $149 plan. With job finding added, the $199 plan comes to about $0.60 an application. With both add-ons, it comes to about $0.79, and the $149 plan to about $1.23. Those sums assume an add-on bills with each month, which the page does not say. Its one-time packages work out to $0.80, $0.60 and about $0.67 an application. Scout's Focused Search is $299 for 250 applications, about $1.20 each, and Full Search is $499 for 500, about $1.00 each, with job finding included. If the lowest published price per application for human-completed work is your main criterion, Scale.jobs' published numbers favor it on most plans.</p>
  <p>What you get for Scout's higher price is the Human route as Scout describes it on its pricing page: a dedicated Human Assistant, a dedicated WhatsApp group, dashboard tracking, the resume used for every job, and screenshots of important form answers, with a second assistant and a weekly campaign review on Career Campaign. Scale.jobs' pages also list human assistants and team chat, and its pricing page promises a proof screenshot for every application, so the two services overlap more than they differ. We have not tested Scale.jobs, and neither page tells you how good the work is, so this comparison covers published prices and listed features only. Compare what is included, what proof you get and how each team communicates before you decide. For a longer side-by-side, see <a href="/compare/scale-jobs-alternative">Scout compared with Scale.jobs</a>.</p>
</section>
